        <h1 class="font-typewriter text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl mb-6">
          Chai latte near Platja d'Aro: what's out there and what's worth it
        </h1>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none font-mono leading-relaxed">

<p class="mb-4">If you've searched for chai latte in Platja d'Aro, you've probably encountered versions made with syrup. A splash of sweet concentrate in warm milk. It works, but it's not the same as a masala chai made with a real spice blend.</p>
<p class="mb-4">The difference isn't subtle. Cardamom, cinnamon, ginger, clove, black pepper — together, in proportion. That's what real chai tastes like.</p>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">What makes a good chai latte</h3>
<ol class="list-decimal list-outside ml-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
  <li>The spices have to actually be there. A properly made chai uses a masala blend — cardamom, cinnamon, ginger, clove, and pepper — not a sweetened concentrate from a bottle.</li>
  <li>The supplier matters. The chai we use at Dirty Rabbit is from Awachai, a producer in Isère, France, with a 100% organic blend. Not what you'll find at most chains.</li>
  <li>Cold works just as well. Iced chai isn't just a summer option — we have it available year-round because the spices hold up perfectly cold.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">Where to find good chai latte near Platja d'Aro</h3>
<p class="mb-4">Dirty Rabbit is in S'Agaró, Avinguda Platja d'Aro 275 — about 10 minutes by car from central Platja d'Aro.</p>
<p class="mb-4">We opened on 1 November 2024. Awachai's organic masala chai has been on the menu from day one. We serve it three ways: classic chai latte (hot or iced), iced chai year-round, and dirty chai — which is the chai latte with a shot of La Cabra espresso. That last one is something. Plant milk available in all versions. Price: €3.50 to €5.</p>
<p class="mb-4">In central Platja d'Aro there are cafés. Good for sitting out with seafront views. For chai made with real spices, the 10-minute detour is worth it.</p>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">Why chai latte is everywhere but good chai is rare</h3>
<p class="mb-4">Chai latte became popular in Spain well before matcha. That has upsides and downsides. Upside: you can order it almost anywhere. Downside: most versions going around are syrup in warm milk, which has little to do with what masala chai actually is.</p>
<p class="mb-4">The problem is cost and interest. A quality organic spice blend costs more than a bottle of concentrate, and many places don't believe the customer will notice the difference. Sometimes they're right. But anyone who's had chai with real spices notices.</p>
<hr class="my-8 border-black/20" />
<h2 class="font-typewriter text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-8 mt-16">Frequently asked questions about chai latte near Platja d'Aro</h2>
<div class="space-y-6">
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Is there anywhere near Platja d'Aro that serves chai with real spices instead of syrup?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Most versions in central Platja d'Aro use syrup or concentrate. The nearest option with real organic masala chai is Dirty Rabbit in S'Agaró, about 10 minutes away.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">How much does a chai latte cost in the area?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">At Dirty Rabbit, between €3.50 and €5 depending on the version. Classic chai latte is at the lower end; dirty chai (with espresso) is at the top.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Can I order iced chai outside of summer?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Yes. At Dirty Rabbit iced chai is available year-round. The masala spices work just as well cold — it's not a seasonal version.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">What is dirty chai and is it worth ordering?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">It's a chai latte with an added shot of espresso. The coffee is from La Cabra (Madrid). It's a strange combination in theory and a very good one in practice — for anyone who wants the energy of coffee but with spice flavour rather than pure bitterness.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Where exactly is Dirty Rabbit?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Avinguda Platja d'Aro 275, S'Agaró. On the main road connecting Sant Feliu with Platja d'Aro. Easy parking across the road, large terrace, WiFi, good morning light.</p>
</div>
<hr class="my-8 border-black/20" />
</div>
<h2 class="font-typewriter text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6 mt-12">About Dirty Rabbit</h2>
<p class="mb-4">We opened on 1 November 2024 in S'Agaró. Iwonka runs day-to-day with a clear rule: every ingredient has to have an explanation — where it comes from, why that supplier.</p>
<p class="mb-4">Chai from Awachai (Isère, France). Coffee from La Cabra. Bread from Origo Bakery. Large terrace, WiFi, good natural light in the mornings. A place where you can stay the whole morning without any issue.</p>

